'''Intrepid Cats''' (導かれしネコ達 ''Michibi Kareshi Neko-tachi,'' '''The Cats Who Are Shown the Way''') is the 29th sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 5.1 Update|Version 5.1]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
This sub-chapter's difficulty really depends on your cats (and their levels). A lot of these stages are very hard and should not be underestimated. And as you may already know, this sub-chapter has [[Darkweb]], notorious for its [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]] and melee pushers! Don't worry, though. It's not hard if you have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]]'s [[True Form]]. But if you don't have good [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|units that neutralize Waves]] or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune attackers]], well heavens above, this is going to be one hell of a sub-chapter for you. Darkweb aside, the hardest stage is probably [[Thorny Dialogue]], a timed stage that can be difficult without high-level cats or [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]].
{{LegendDiff|120|140|100}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces two new enemies:
*[[Tackey]]: A [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy with the [[Long Distance]] ability. Its crushing attacks hit a small area ahead of it with a large blind spot and can wipe out your units with ease.
*[[Mr. Angel]]: A shorter-ranged [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of [[Trolly Blogger]] with much higher overall stats, more than double movement speed and the ability to [[Weaken|weaken]] cats in place of Trolly Blogger's [[Knockback|knockback]].

