==Trivia==
*Intrepid Cats' Japanese name, Michibi Kareshi Neko-tachi (導かれしネコ達, "The Cats Who Are Shown the Way"), is probably a reference to ''[https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_IV:_Chapters_of_the_Chosen Dragon Quest IV]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s Japanese title, ''Michibi Kareshi Mono-tachi'' (導かれし者たち, "The People Who Are Shown the Way").
*Most the stages' names relate to the enemies appearing in them:
**[[Mysterious Order]]'s Japanese name, Mystery Circle (ミステリーサークル), is the Japanese term for [[wikipedia:Crop circle|crop circles]], referencing both the [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] and [[Metal Doge]], who became a cyborg after an incident involving a silver disc in the sky.
**[[Birdwatching]] consists of [[Duche]]s and [[R.Ost]]s.
**[[Thorny Dialogue]] introduces [[Tackey]], who fires thorny projectiles from its mouth.
**[[Darkweb]]'s Japanese name, Black Wave (ブラックウェーブ), hints that there are [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]], and [[Two Can]], who is both.
*Intrepid Cats is the only main sub-chapter in [[Legend Stages]] to have five stages.
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], this may have initially been planned to be added into the game as there are sprites in the game's files, but was most likely scrapped in favoring [[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]]'s [[Dead End Night]] sub-chapter to be the final chapter in-game.

